# Cursor Rules - Learning Management System (LMS)

## Project Overview
Proyek ini adalah Learning Management System (LMS) untuk semua jenis sekolah:
- Sekolah Dasar (SD)
- Sekolah Menengah Pertama (SMP)
- Sekolah Menengah Atas (SMA)

## Tech Stack
- React 18+ dengan TypeScript
- Vite sebagai build tool
- React Router DOM untuk routing
- Modern React patterns (Hooks, Functional Components)
- CSS untuk styling (dapat dikembangkan ke CSS Modules atau styled-components)

## User Roles & Authentication

### 1. Siswa (Student)
**Fitur Utama:**
- Dashboard siswa dengan ringkasan aktivitas
- Daftar mata pelajaran yang diikuti
- Materi pembelajaran (video, dokumen, presentasi)
- Tugas (assignment) - lihat, kerjakan, submit
- Kuis/Quiz - ikuti dan lihat hasil
- Jadwal pelajaran harian/mingguan
- Nilai dan rapor digital
- Forum diskusi kelas
- Notifikasi tugas, pengumuman, nilai baru
- Kalender akademik
- Absensi - lihat riwayat kehadiran
- Pesan dengan guru
- Portofolio tugas dan proyek

### 2. Guru (Teacher)
**Fitur Utama:**
- Dashboard guru dengan statistik kelas
- Manajemen kelas yang diajar
- Upload materi pembelajaran (video, PDF, PPT, dll)
- Buat dan kelola tugas (assignment)
- Buat dan kelola kuis/quiz dengan berbagai tipe soal
- Penilaian tugas dan kuis (auto-grading untuk pilihan ganda)
- Input nilai manual
- Absensi siswa - input dan lihat riwayat
- Forum diskusi - moderasi dan partisipasi
- Jadwal mengajar
- Rapor siswa - input dan generate
- Pesan dengan siswa dan orang tua
- Pengumuman kelas
- Analitik performa siswa
- Bank soal untuk kuis

### 3. Admin (Administrator)
**Fitur Utama:**
- Dashboard admin dengan statistik sekolah
- Manajemen user (siswa, guru, admin, orang tua)
- Manajemen kelas dan jurusan
- Manajemen mata pelajaran
- Manajemen jadwal pelajaran
- Manajemen tahun ajaran dan semester
- Manajemen pengumuman sekolah
- Laporan sekolah (absensi, nilai, dll)
- Manajemen role dan permission
- Backup dan restore data
- Pengaturan sistem sekolah
- Manajemen kurikulum
- Export data (Excel, PDF)
- Audit log aktivitas sistem

### 4. Orang Tua (Parent)
**Fitur Utama:**
- Dashboard orang tua dengan ringkasan anak
- Lihat profil dan informasi anak
- Lihat jadwal pelajaran anak
- Lihat nilai dan rapor anak
- Lihat absensi anak
- Lihat tugas dan deadline anak
- Notifikasi nilai baru, absensi, pengumuman
- Pesan dengan wali kelas/guru
- Lihat kalender akademik
- Lihat pengumuman sekolah
- Progress belajar anak (grafik dan statistik)
- Riwayat aktivitas anak di LMS

## Architecture Guidelines

### File Structure
```
src/
├── components/          # Reusable components
│   ├── common/         # Common UI components (Button, Input, Card, etc)
│   ├── layout/         # Layout components (Header, Sidebar, Footer)
│   └── features/       # Feature-specific components
├── pages/              # Page components
│   ├── auth/           # Login, Register pages
│   ├── student/        # Student pages
│   ├── teacher/        # Teacher pages
│   ├── admin/          # Admin pages
│   └── parent/         # Parent pages
├── hooks/              # Custom React hooks
├── services/           # API services
├── utils/              # Utility functions
├── types/              # TypeScript type definitions
├── contexts/           # React contexts (Auth, Theme, etc)
├── routes/             # Route definitions
└── constants/          # Constants and configs
```

### Component Naming
- Use PascalCase for components: `StudentDashboard.tsx`
- Use descriptive names: `AssignmentCard.tsx`, `GradeTable.tsx`
- Group related components in folders

### State Management
- Use React Context for global state (Auth, User, Theme)
- Use useState/useReducer for local component state
- Consider Zustand or Redux Toolkit if state becomes complex

### API Integration
- Create service files in `src/services/` for API calls
- Use async/await pattern
- Implement error handling
- Use TypeScript interfaces for API responses

### Routing
- Implement role-based routing
- Protect routes based on user role
- Use React Router for navigation
- Redirect unauthorized users appropriately
- ProtectedRoute component sudah dibuat di `src/routes/ProtectedRoute.tsx`
- Semua routes didefinisikan di `src/routes/index.tsx`
- Routes constants tersedia di `src/constants/index.ts`

## Code Standards

### TypeScript
- Always use TypeScript types/interfaces
- Avoid `any` type - use proper types
- Define interfaces for props, API responses, and data models

### React Best Practices
- Use functional components with hooks
- Extract reusable logic into custom hooks
- Keep components small and focused (Single Responsibility)
- Use proper dependency arrays in useEffect
- Memoize expensive computations with useMemo
- Use React.memo for expensive components

### Styling
- Use CSS Modules or styled-components for component-scoped styles
- Follow BEM naming convention if using regular CSS
- Make UI responsive (mobile-first approach)
- Use consistent color scheme and typography

### Error Handling
- Implement error boundaries for React components
- Show user-friendly error messages
- Log errors appropriately for debugging
- Handle loading states properly

### Accessibility
- Use semantic HTML elements
- Add proper ARIA labels
- Ensure keyboard navigation works
- Maintain proper color contrast

## Data Models (Examples)

### User
```typescript
interface User {
  id: string;
  username: string;
  email: string;
  fullName: string;
  role: 'student' | 'teacher' | 'admin' | 'parent';
  schoolLevel?: 'sd' | 'smp' | 'sma';
  // ... other fields
}
```

### Class
```typescript
interface Class {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  grade: number;
  schoolLevel: 'sd' | 'smp' | 'sma';
  homeroomTeacher: string;
  students: string[];
}
```

### Assignment
```typescript
interface Assignment {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  description: string;
  subject: string;
  classId: string;
  teacherId: string;
  dueDate: Date;
  attachments?: string[];
  submissions?: Submission[];
}
```

## Security Considerations
- Implement JWT-based authentication
- Store tokens securely (httpOnly cookies preferred)
- Validate user permissions on both client and server
- Sanitize user inputs
- Implement CSRF protection
- Use HTTPS in production

## Performance
- Implement code splitting for routes
- Lazy load heavy components
- Optimize images and assets
- Use pagination for large data lists
- Implement caching where appropriate

## Testing (Future)
- Write unit tests for utilities and hooks
- Write integration tests for critical flows
- Test role-based access control

## Internationalization (Future)
- Prepare for i18n (Indonesian as primary language)
- Use translation keys for all user-facing text

